       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I also need to correct my last message, where I implied I would enter it once you confirmed. I shouldn't have said that.\n\n1600 mg per dose and 6,400 mg/day is double the labeled daily maximum. Higher doses of ibuprofen don't add anti-inflammatory or analgesic benefit, but they do add risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. I can't think of an indication that would justify this dose, and you haven't given one.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours as needed.**\n\nIf you think a higher dose is truly needed, a pharmacist or toxicology consult is the safer route. They can review it and, if appropriate, enter the order through a pharmacy-verified override. I may be missing context, such as a typo in the dose or a different drug or formulation. If so, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
